        <h3>Why Worldwide Government, Consular &amp; Creator Portals Enforce Strict Limits</h3>
        <p>
          To understand why exact file optimization is required, consider the operational constraints of large institutional portals. When national testing agencies (like SSC, UPSC, NTA, or IBPS) or immigration authorities (such as the US Department of State CEAC portal, UK Visas &amp; Immigration UKVI, Schengen VFS Global, or Canada IRCC) open an application window, their ingest pipelines process millions of digital submissions within narrow deadlines.
        </p>
        <p>
          Similarly, major digital platforms enforce strict binary ceilings to optimize content delivery networks (CDNs). YouTube caps thumbnails at 2MB, Discord limits free tier file uploads to 8MB and emojis to 256KB, while WhatsApp heavily compresses status photos unless pre-optimized to clean aspect ratios. Pre-compressing assets ensures rapid delivery without losing visual fidelity.
